}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶z\n$$\n\n \n\nand is twice differentiable at $x=a.$ Then, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]|}_{x=a}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(a)={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]}_{x=a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}], & \\,{f}^{″}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial:\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2y} & 2{e}^{x+2y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {f}^{′}(0,0) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the second derivative, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2y} & 2{e}^{x+2y} \\\\ 2{e}^{x+2y} & 4{e}^{x+2y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {f}^{″}(0,0) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the sum of the missing expressions is\n\n$$\n1+2+x+x+2+x=3x+5.\n$$" 13194139535776 true] [17592186198582 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535776 true] [17592186198582 1100 "For the function of two variables\n\n$f(x, y) = \\cos (x - 2y)$,\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0, 0)$ is given by\n$f(x, y) = 1 + ax^{2} + bxy + cy^{2}$.\nFind the value of $a + b + c$." 13194139535776 false] [17592186198582 1100 "For the function of two variables \n$f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2y),$\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=1+a{x}^{2}+bxy+c{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" 13194139535776 true] [17592186198582 1145 "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at $(x,y)=(0,0),$ then the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈\\overset{\\text{Linear approximation}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(0,0)+{f}_{x}(0,0)\\cdot x+{f}_{y}(0,0)\\cdot y}} \\\\  & \\,\\,+{{\\frac{1}{2}({f}_{xx}(0,0)\\cdot {x}^{2}+2{f}_{xy}(0,0)\\cdot xy+{f}_{yy}(0,0)\\cdot {y}^{2})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Quadratic part}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-2y), & \\,{f}_{y}(x,y) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{x}(0,0) & =0, & \\,{f}_{y}(0,0) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the second derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2y), & \\,{f}_{xx}(0,0) & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2y), & \\,{f}_{xy}(0,0) & =2 \\\\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2y), & \\,{f}_{yy}(0,0) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈1+0\\cdot x+0\\cdot y+\\frac{1}{2}(-1\\cdot {x}^{2}+2(2)\\cdot xy+(-4)\\cdot {y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1+(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{2}+2xy+(-2){y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=(-\\frac{1}{2})+2+(-2)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365648 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1089 "q-163088" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1100 "For the function of two variables \n$f(x,y)={e}^{xy},$\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=a+bxy.\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b.$" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1113 #uuid "09e4111a-d204-5e67-864f-bf2698974078" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365647 1145 "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at $(x,y)=(0,0),$ then the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈\\overset{\\text{Linear approximation}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(0,0)+{f}_{x}(0,0)\\cdot x+{f}_{y}(0,0)\\cdot y}} \\\\  & \\,\\,+{{\\frac{1}{2}({f}_{xx}(0,0)\\cdot {x}^{2}+2{f}_{xy}(0,0)\\cdot xy+{f}_{yy}(0,0)\\cdot {y}^{2})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Quadratic part}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =y{e}^{xy}, & \\,{f}_{y}(x,y) & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ {f}_{x}(0,0) & =0, & \\,{f}_{y}(0,0) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the second derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}, & \\,{f}_{xx}(0,0) & =0 \\\\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =(1+xy){e}^{xy}, & \\,{f}_{xy}(0,0) & =1 \\\\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & ={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}, & \\,{f}_{yy}(0,0) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈1+0\\cdot x+0\\cdot y+\\frac{1}{2}(0\\cdot {x}^{2}+2(1)\\cdot xy+0\\cdot {y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1+1xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b=1+1=2.\n$$" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365649 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365650 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365651 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365652 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365653 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1041 "selection" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365650 13194139535776 true] [17592186365648 1110 #uuid "8ddfd091-fe4f-54a2-b3ba-53ceedbdb333" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365649 1034 "3" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535776 true] [17592186365649 1111 #uuid "dd867988-d331-5df8-a217-a6e6d2d4cf48" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365650 1034 "2" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535776 true] [17592186365650 1111 #uuid "1bf2438e-0e53-5cd5-9d54-2682ae6286ce" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365651 1034 "4" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535776 true] [17592186365651 1111 #uuid "d67fa04c-5935-541d-8571-73ebca3d2660" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365652 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535776 true] [17592186365652 1111 #uuid "f34fb7f1-dc69-558f-abbc-8b4e1dff2ebb" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365653 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535776 true] [17592186365653 1111 #uuid "6700134e-b52b-56f8-b098-58eca236ad2b" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365654 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365655 13194139535776 true] [17592186365654 1089 "q-163089" 13194139535776 true] [17592186365654 1091 #edb/ref 175921860